# oracle: examples/PACKAGES/mgpt/in.vac0-bcc (unrelaxed vacancy in a 5x5x5 bcc Ta crystal, 249 atoms, Ta6.8x MGPT potential at the 249-site lattice volume) up to its run 0, with the energy and pressure the example prints
# native: b332f28 built with -D PKG_MGPT=on -D PKG_MANYBODY=on -D PKG_MOLECULE=on (serial, 1 process, default CMake Release flags, so the MGPT generic linear algebra; the installed lmp lacks MGPT)
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 1.1e-15, atoms 0 (bit for bit).
# oracle-potentials: Ta6.8x.mgpt.parmin Ta6.8x.mgpt.potin
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           electron
atom_style      atomic
variable        atomic_vol equal 121.6
variable        lat_vol equal ${atomic_vol}*249/250
variable        lattice_constant equal (${lat_vol}*2.0)^(1.0/3.0)
lattice         bcc ${lattice_constant}
region          box block 0 5 0 5 0 5
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
region vacancy sphere 2.5 2.5 2.5 0.1 units lattice
delete_atoms region vacancy
pair_style      mgpt
pair_coeff      * * Ta6.8x.mgpt.parmin Ta6.8x.mgpt.potin  ${atomic_vol}
velocity        all create 0.0 87287
neighbor        0.1 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
fix             1 all nve
variable        natoms equal "count(all)"
variable        etotry equal "2.0*pe/v_natoms"
variable        ptotgpa equal "press/1.0e+09"
thermo          10
thermo_style    custom step vol temp pe etotal press v_etotry v_ptotgpa
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             0
